title: Letters from Prison
subtitle: A comrade writes from his cell.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month >= 9 and month <= 11 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and e21_prison_done = 0 and (comrade_brandler = 2 or comrade_hoelz = 2)
max-visits: 1
priority: 5
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_prison_done = 1;
Q.e21_prison_outcome = 0;
Q.e21_prison_id = (Q.comrade_brandler == 2) ? 'brandler' : 'hoelz';
Q.e21_prison_brandler = (Q.e21_prison_id == 'brandler') ? 1 : 0;
Q.e21_prison_name = RG.comradeName(Q.e21_prison_id);
// the Hoelz campaign has made friends among the warders
Q.e21_escape_p = (Q.e21_prison_brandler == 1) ? 0.7 : (Q.e21_hoelz_campaign == 1 ? 0.4 : 0.2);
Q.e21_escape_odds = (Q.e21_escape_p >= 0.6) ? 3 : ((Q.e21_escape_p >= 0.35) ? 2 : 1);
!}

= Letters from Prison

[? if e21_prison_brandler = 1 : Heinrich Brandler writes from the fortress where the special court sent him for signing the call to arms in March. The letters come out folded into the hems of his laundry. They are dry and practical, like the man: what the party should say to the metalworkers about wages, and what it should stop saying about the offensive. ?][? if e21_prison_brandler = 0 : Max Hoelz writes from the penitentiary at Münster. He is allowed one letter a month, and he writes ten. They are angry and funny and impossible to edit: about the warders, the judges, and the comrades who called him a bandit. ?]

- @publish: Print them in the Rote Fahne.
- @escape: Get him out.
- @file: Keep them in the Zentrale's files.

@publish
subtitle: [? if e21_prison_brandler = 1 : The union men will read him more closely than they read the Zentrale. ?][? if e21_prison_brandler = 0 : The workers will read every word. So will the prison governor. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_prison_outcome = 1;
Q.worker_support += 2;
if (Q.e21_prison_brandler == 1) {
    Q.lean_unionist += 1;
} else {
    RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 4});
    Q.lean_offensive += 1;
}
!}

The letters run in the Rote Fahne for a week under the heading "From behind bars". [? if e21_prison_brandler = 0 : In the Vogtland they are read aloud in the pubs. ?]

@escape
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. [? if e21_escape_odds = 3 : A fortress is not a prison, and the apparatus thinks it can be done. ?][? if e21_escape_odds = 2 : Some of the Münster warders have been signing the petitions. It might work. ?][? if e21_escape_odds = 1 : Münster is a penitentiary. The apparatus gives it little chance. ?]
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no money for false papers and a car.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
if (Math.random() < Q.e21_escape_p) {
    Q.e21_prison_outcome = 4;
    if (Q.e21_prison_brandler == 1) {
        RG.exile('brandler', {news: 'Brandler escapes to Moscow', priority: 2});
        Q.e21_brandler_escaped = 1;
        RG.ledger('Heinrich Brandler escaped from prison to Moscow.', 'e21_brandler_escape');
    } else {
        RG.exile('hoelz', {news: 'Max Hoelz escapes from Münster', priority: 3});
        RG.ledger('Max Hoelz escaped from the penitentiary at Münster.', 'e21_hoelz_escape');
    }
} else {
    Q.e21_prison_outcome = 5;
    Q.repression += 4;
    RG.news('Escape plot foiled: ' + Q.e21_prison_name + ' moved to a stricter prison', 2);
}
!}

[? if e21_prison_outcome = 4 and e21_prison_brandler = 1 : A warder is paid, a car waits on a country road, and a week later Brandler is in Stettin with a Latvian passport. By Christmas he is in Moscow, where the Executive gives him a desk. ?][? if e21_prison_outcome = 4 and e21_prison_brandler = 0 : Hoelz goes over the wall on a rope of sheets. He is hidden in Saxony, and then smuggled abroad. ?][? if e21_prison_outcome = 5 : The plan is betrayed by a prisoner who wanted a shorter sentence. The warders find the rope and the police find the car. ?]

@file
subtitle: The courts read the Rote Fahne too. He will think we have forgotten him.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_prison_outcome = 6;
if (Q.e21_prison_brandler == 1) { Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 6; } else { Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 6; }
!}

The letters go into a drawer, and Red Aid sends parcels. [+ e21_prison_name +] stops writing to the Zentrale and writes only to his friends.
